AB  - Eleanor Pickford ep646 Mon, 10/08/2026 - 09:03 I am a PhD candidate working primarily on the history of political thought in the medieval period. My dissertation examines the themes of utopia and ideality through texts by authors including John of Salisbury, Christine de Pizan and Dante Alighieri. In light of the limited presence of the medieval period in scholarship on utopia, I am interested in how authors such as these conceived of the possibilities and limits of human agency and how these conceptions were expressed in their visions of political communities. My interest in utopia extends…
